Rules of Evidence
-When evaluating evidence in order to make a decision of competence, the assessor must ensure that the evidence provide satisfies the Rules of Evidence

Valid
-To ensure... PUCHA!!!


Authentic
--Authenticity relates to ensuring that each piece of evidence is from the candidate and not another person - that the assessor is confident that it is the candidates own work.

Current
--Curency relates to the age of the evidence presented by a candidate to demonstrate that they are still competent.

Sufficient
--Sufficiency relates to the quality and quantity of evidence assessed. It requires collection of enough appropriate evidence to ensure that all aspects of competency have been satisfied.

Consistent
-Does the evience show that the candidate consistently meets the standards under workplace conditions rather that showing a one-off demonstration of the standards
-Incorporate multiple items of evidence

